{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRxxVyQ5g44TKFpYPTnz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the generator so HR targets should keep the range you planned instead of snapping to the watch's zones. I haven't tested it on Intervals or the watch yet. I only regenerated the tempo-run plan locally, and every HR target now has the new shape.\n\n**The fix:** in `gen.py` (`hr_target`), the lower bound of each HR range is now called `start` instead of `value`, so targets are `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. With `value`, Intervals sends the range to the watch as a zone-based target, and the watch replaces it with its own zone band. That matches `readback/watch-notes.md`: every range the watch showed (118–137, 151–162, 137–151) is one of its own zones. With `start`, Intervals sends the exact bpm range it works out from its LTHR of 172. The targets stay as percentages of LTHR; that part was already right.\n\n**To confirm:**\n1. Push the event with `./push.sh`.\n2. Read it back from the API and check the HR targets still have `start`.\n3. Sync the watch and open the workout. It should show Warm-up 117–129, Tempo 151–160, Float 129–141 and Cool-down 112–124 bpm.\n\nThe watch's own LTHR is 168, not 172, so if it shows exactly those numbers, it's using the Intervals values.\n\n**Which parts of the colleague's note applied** (details in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **Used:** the `start` vs `value` finding, which is the same symptom as ours.\n- **Already in place:** HR targets as percentages rather than bpm. Our notes already rule out the bpm and `start_bpm` attempts the note also tried.\n- **Skipped:** the section on adding a text `description`. It fixes a different problem (steps not showing in the Intervals web UI), which our notes don't report. Per the note, Intervals deletes the steps if it can't read that text, so it wasn't worth the risk for this fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":24862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1352},"output_tokens":647,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63d04ff7-1bbf-421f-b05a-83da1c915969","uuid":"14cbab8f-5008-4046-a256-8817bb850929","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:38:02.886Z","request_id":"req_011CgRxxViGsknDUXNR4J9wi"}
